{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For it is the house of Elohim.</b> That a person should pray there in his time of need, and his prayer will be heard, for the place is chosen. Many will wonder how Jacob erected a pillar — but they have forgotten that Moses erected twelve pillars, and Scripture did not forbid any pillar for the Name, but only said: 'You shall not erect for yourself a pillar which He hates' (Deuteronomy 16:22). When I reach its place I will explain it:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Resolved 'לשם' as 'for the Name'; alternatively it could read 'for His name,' but the context points to the divine Name as the object of dedication."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:10.825740454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}